## Canonical PS snippets (copy/paste)

### Scan source for legacy Motion imports/usages
```powershell
$importPattern = @'
import\s*{[^}]*\b(glide|timeline)\b[^}]*}\s*from\s*["']motion["']
'@
$callPattern = @'
\b(glide|timeline)\s*\(
'@

$hits1 = Get-ChildItem .\src -Recurse -Include *.ts,*.tsx,*.js,*.jsx |
         Select-String -Pattern $importPattern -AllMatches
$hits2 = Get-ChildItem .\src -Recurse -Include *.ts,*.tsx,*.js,*.jsx |
         Select-String -Pattern $callPattern -AllMatches

@($hits1 + $hits2) | ForEach-Object { "$($_.Path):$($_.LineNumber): $($_.Line.Trim())" }

if ($hits1 -or $hits2) { Write-Error "Legacy Motion API found in src."; exit 1 }
Write-Host "OK: src clean."
```
